## Executed code and isolation

The harness copied the actual source files and installed engine to an owned
scratch fixture, then bundled the new portable module and real SDK receipt
exports with esbuild. The 11-module graph and every input's bytes/hash are
recorded; receipt, native engine and Astronomy Engine are present, geo and
ownership SDK are absent. All 23 installed rc.5 package members and fixture
copies match the exact vendored archive. Astronomy Engine is 2.1.19.

The final 125,683-byte bundle has SHA256
`33f8bb250e61a39b986b2f1d4acc2e73f4a1ee4926e35c60027234cec5416515`.
Final runner SHA256:
`baf3dd5efeb41c3ff3267e347441d2bcd7cddce12489164667652bbee8cee685`.
Final browser-cases SHA256:
`c1e84b97e3aa92f5c1f24d7db6b5db9bb7ccc77588403389c87f0125a5ff1dab`.

Only three local static GETs loaded the owned page, bundle and test cases. The
page then ran with browser networking offline and a deny rule for further
requests. There were zero subsequent requests, request failures, console errors,
page errors or observed calculation-time network/storage/cookie/Intl calls.
Local/session storage and cookies were empty before and after. Observer negative
controls throw before performing their synthetic network or storage operations.

The 42 negative controls cover fetch, XHR, WebSocket, EventSource, workers,
beacons, local/session storage methods, IndexedDB, CacheStorage, cookies,
every available Intl function entry (13 in this Chrome), and six locale-format
shortcuts on Date/Number/BigInt/String. The exact list and observed events are
recorded. This is measured coverage of those browser interfaces, not a claim to
sandbox arbitrary code or authenticate caller metadata.

## Runtime cases

The actual browser executed complete native calculation and receipt creation,
compared all compact body/angle/house/aspect values at full precision, retained
requested Placidus versus actual Whole, preserved unknown-time 08:30 and explicit
source ISO spelling, serialized and parsed the frozen receipt, and checked the
canonical replay input. Mutation controls changed every mutable chart branch,
caller Date/flags/context, and attempted writes into recursively frozen outputs.

Further cases cover fixed private errors without raw error inspection, revoked
context proxies, context accessors/oversize data, one-read input getters,
post-calculation context capture, explicit historical-resolution metadata,
missing-place/unknown-time-noon distinctions, and year 0099 handling. The receipt
remains a Zodiacs draft and its provenance remains claimed.

This is an owned synthetic acceptance page, not product UI or a saved/account
workflow. `initial-page.png` and `offline-results.png` were inspected; content is
visible, the 12 successful groups render, and no error overlay appeared. Raw
coverage, browser trace, source/module identities and request records are kept.
No new numerical oracle, human review, broad accuracy certification, account
migration acceptance, production deployment or external adoption is claimed.

## Attempts and cleanup

The first run (`run-1788841801131-17555`) passed the same 12 runtime groups and
24 observer controls. It measured DateTimeFormat specifically. Its runner,
browser cases, raw results and captures are retained separately. The final
harness added all available Intl entries and locale shortcuts; product source
was unchanged and no tolerance or acceptance assertion was weakened.

Both runs closed their owned browser and server and removed their owned profile.
After interruption, the final result and source identities remained intact, no
owned process remained, and the profile was absent. The initial process-inspection
attempt was blocked by the filesystem/process sandbox's `ps` permission; an
escalated read-only inspection succeeded. This was not a candidate browser failure
or an automatic approval-review rejection. `post-interruption-check.json` records
that check. No rerun was needed after the interruption, and no other browser view
or separate Astrofolio work was inspected or changed.

Reproduce from the frozen root source and implementation identity using the exact
command in `final-command.json`. The runner writes only under its evidence
folder and refuses source/artifact mismatches. Bundle path comments, ephemeral
ports and timestamps change between runs, so compare recorded source and module
bytes as well as each run's own bundle hash. `copy-manifest.json` maps selected
raw evidence into durable docs without formatting or executable test discovery;
fixture dependency duplicates are excluded because their exact members are
already identified against the archived package and recorded in the module graph.
